refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.returnvalues;


 Returns the previously defined exception handler, or &null; on error. If
 no previous handler was defined, &null; is also returned.

&reftitle.changelog;
&Version; &Description;
8.3.5
The exception handler being invoked is now pushed onto the handler stack and re-installed once it returns, unless the handler modified the stack itself.
8.3.0
The active exception handler is now unset while it runs, so set_exception_handler called from within a handler reports no previously defined handler.

  &reftitle.examples;



    set_exception_handler example


<?php
function exception_handler(Throwable $exception) {
  echo "Uncaught exception: " , $exception->getMessage(), "\n";
}

set_exception_handler('exception_handler');

throw new Exception('Uncaught Exception');
echo "Not Executed\n";
?>
